\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. The duteous day now closeth \tab 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Each flower and tree reposeth
\par Shade creeps o'er wild and wood
\par Let us as night is falling
\par On God our Maker calling
\par Give thanks to Him, the Giver good
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Now all the heavenly splendour
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Breaks forth in starlight tender
\par From myriad worlds unknown
\par And man the marvel seeing
\par Forgets his selfish being
\par \pard\li45\sl190\slmult0     For joy of beauty not his own \tab\tab 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  His care he drowneth yonder
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Lost in the abyss of wonder
\par To heaven his soul doth steal
\par This life he disesteemeth
\par The day it is that dreameth
\par That doth from truth his vision seal.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   Awhile his mortal blindness
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 May miss God's loving-kindness
\par And grope in faithless strife
\par But, when life's day is over
\par Shall death's fair night discover
\par \pard       The fields of everlasting life.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

